                <pb facs="0897" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg801"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 930.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ruelas to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 29,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: With reference to my note dated
                    the 12th of this month, I have the honor to remit to your excellency a copy of a
                    communication from the department of war, in which I am informed that the forces
                    at Mier and Laredo have moved in pursuit of the Lipans that were threatening the
                    State of Texas. I improve this opportunity to renew to your excellency the
                    assurances of my distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>M. RUELAS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
